WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:07.240
It's Rob Lucci!

3
00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.990
Then it's true. They came here to kill
Vegapunk, just as he feared that they would.

4
00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:15.500
Who the hell invited you, Pigeon Guy?
You get outta here!

5
00:00:17.860 --> 00:00:18.880
Go!

6
00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:20.540
This is a Government island.

7
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.210
Oh crap, you're right!

8
00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.300
We're the ones who aren't
supposed to be here!

9
00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:27.720
Ah! Will you focus? None of that matters!

10
00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.300
Come on, Luffy! We gotta get
to the upper level, now!

11
00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.640
The Straw Hats, huh?

12
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:34.560
Didn't know this place had a pest problem.

13
00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.930
Jewelry Bonney, too.

14
00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.350
But we can't do anything yet, Lucci!

15
00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:44.820
Remember, Straw Hat is an Emperor of the Sea now,
We can't fight him without permission from the top.

16
00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.400
He's right.

17
00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.950
The Four Emperors often have powerful allies.

18
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:51.570
One little scuffle could lead to a war.

19
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.830
Send a report to the Navy now.

20
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:54.580
Roger!

21
00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.830
I'm not sure we can avoid a fight so easily.

22
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:04.040
Gotta go, Jinbe! Hold Bonney!

23
00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.390
Luffy, what's the matter?

24
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.640
What happened?

25
00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:19.640
Wait, I know her!

26
00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:21.850
It's that girl from before!

27
00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.650
Chopper! Help her, please!

28
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.570
I'm sorry, but. I think
this is more Franky's specialty than mine!

29
00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.420
This is Government business.

30
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.440
You would be wise to stay out of it.

31
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.010
She fed us. She took care of us when we
came here, and that makes her a friend!

32
00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:33.650
<b>Marine Headquarters</b>

33
00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:33.650
The straw hats are on Egghead?

34
00:03:33.650 --> 00:03:35.110
Why, dammit?

35
00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:36.490
See this?

36
00:03:37.110 --> 00:03:40.410
You give people an inch
and they give you nothing but a headache.

37
00:03:40.700 --> 00:03:45.540
He must have figured out that CP0 was there
to kill them. That's not a good sign.

38
00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:49.630
Yes, sir. That's likely why they had
to use S-Bear to teleport inside.

39
00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:54.340
And what they did is declare war.

40
00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:59.800
I wish they'd had the common sense
to contact... Me first! Those arrogant brats.

41
00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.060
If Vegapunk has the Straw Hats on his side,
this could be a real disaster.

42
00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:07.020
Who knows how many good Marines we could lose.

43
00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:09.980
Where's Kizaru?

44
00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:12.270
He's on his way to Egghead right now.

45
00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:16.030
He was already en route
in service of a different mission.

46
00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:20.240
Tell Lucci to avoid any further action
until backup arrives.

47
00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.160
Sir!

48
00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:26.080
No matter what happens,
we cannot let him fight Straw Hat!

49
00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.870
<b>Egghead
New World</b>

50
00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:31.580
Intruder alert! Evacuate immediately!

51
00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:34.050
<b>The Strongest Form of Humanity</b>

52
00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.460
I repeat, evacuate immediately!

53
00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:36.460
You take Bonney, I'll take her.

54
00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:39.840
Ah, We need to get her to Franky right away.

55
00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.760
You ready, Luffy?

56
00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:48.640
Go on without me.

57
00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.880
What was that form in your wanted poster?

58
00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:06.550
What, you wanna see it?

59
00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:08.560
Do you need to ask?

60
00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:49.680
I feel it, I feel it, I feel it, I feel it!

61
00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:51.140
What the hell?

62
00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:45.190
I'll be damned.

63
00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:47.030
This should be fun.

64
00:08:09.010 --> 00:08:10.050
Lucci.

65
00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.020
Hey, yoo-hoo,

66
00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:21.230
Pigeon guy,

67
00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:24.320
get over here! Let's fight some more!

68
00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.830
Still playing games,
even when your life is on the line?

69
00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:37.160
I'm starting to get annoyed.

70
00:09:08.160 --> 00:09:10.790
Don't get cocky, Straw Hat.

71
00:09:11.200 --> 00:09:16.740
I've gotten stronger, just like you have.
All the better to eat prey like you alive.

72
00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:16.740
<b>Cat-Cat Fruit: Leopard
Awakened Form</b>

73
00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:20.920
Wait, something's different!

74
00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:23.580
He definitely didn't look like that before!

75
00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:28.550
Stop, Lucci! We don't have
authorization for this!

76
00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.890
His speed is incredible,

77
00:09:34.890 --> 00:09:36.680
but so is his control!

78
00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:40.430
It's rare that an awakened zoan user
can maintain their state of mind.

79
00:10:13.970 --> 00:10:16.050
Please, think of the position you're in!

80
00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.720
The Government will hunt you down for this!

81
00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:27.690
Shaka!

82
00:10:28.070 --> 00:10:30.400
What happened? Did
the white-haired warrior appear?

83
00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.150
Oh my god, real Vegapunk!

84
00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:34.830
How in the hell did he get up here so fast?

85
00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:38.080
Remarkable!

86
00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:41.540
Tell me more! I must know everything
about this transformation!

87
00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:43.750
What is that form?

88
00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:46.130
Well, it's new, so we don't know much, either,

89
00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:48.410
but it's a Gum-Gum thing, right?

90
00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:54.680
That's a Devil Fruit Encyclopedia,

91
00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:59.390
There is no mention of a Gum-Gum Fruit.
This must be something else!

92
00:10:59.390 --> 00:11:00.350
Huh?

93
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.430
Wait, are you saying it's a different devil fruit?

94
00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:06.150
If that's true, then why does he say
Gum-Gum all the time?

95
00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:13.240
He's so beautiful.

96
00:11:14.070 --> 00:11:16.990
There is a figure from the ancient past.

97
00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:19.990
One with the same form
your captain has now!

98
00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.160
A god from the old texts!

99
00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:25.960
A god?

100
00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.420
I'm sorry, Luffy?

101
00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:28.790
Stupid incarnate, Luffy?

102
00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:31.300
Yes.

103
00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:39.040
The Warrior of Liberation.
He who plays the fool and brings smiles to all.

104
00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.810
There's no mistaking him.

105
00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.140
He is the Sun God!

106
00:11:44.140 --> 00:11:44.980
Nika!

107
00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.860
Nika? I've never heard of him.

108
00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:52.480
That's no surprise.

109
00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:55.070
The World Government erased
his name from history.

110
00:11:55.530 --> 00:12:00.820
But as long as people yearn for the Warrior
of Liberation, he will never truly disappear!

111
00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:05.250
For it is desire that brings forth
everything in this world!

112
00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:07.080
Take for example

113
00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.540
the devil fruits and all their power!

114
00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.630
You can see it, can't you?

115
00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:19.050
Each devil fruit is a possibility
for evolution that someone desires!

116
00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:20.840
I wish I could do this.

117
00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.810
I wish I could do that.

118
00:12:22.810 --> 00:12:26.770
All of the powers represent
potential futures of humanity!

119
00:12:27.180 --> 00:12:30.400
But these fantastic possibilities
are not a natural

120
00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:35.770
part of this world, so the mother of nature,
the sea, rejects them!

121
00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:38.990
Therefore, you might say...

122
00:12:42.950 --> 00:12:47.610
Those who have powers live
in different realities.

123
00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.690
Realities someone dreamed up!

124
00:12:55.800 --> 00:12:58.260
That is my hypothesis!

125
00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:03.720
One where god's existence is irrelevant!

126
00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.890
What an interesting world, wouldn't you say?

127
00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:17.740
Do those idiots know where they're fighting?
This isn't a playground!

128
00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:20.780
Not for pirates, and not for CP0, either!

129
00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:23.070
<b>Sentomaru
Captain of Marine Headquarters' Science Corps</b>

130
00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:26.040
Why are you bothering me on my day off?

131
00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.870
Why did you take so long to answer?

132
00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.000
Whatever! I'm here, aren't I?

133
00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.330
So what's the plan, Punk?

134
00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.840
Cipher Pol is our ally, and

135
00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:36.300
the pirates are the enemy, right?

136
00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:40.010
Do you want me to just back up CP0, or what?

137
00:13:40.340 --> 00:13:42.930
Quite the opposite, I'm afraid.

138
00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:47.180
CP0 is here to assassinate me,
so I need your help to escape.

139
00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:51.190
Don't get caught up in the details.
Just keep them away!

140
00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.440
I can't do that!

141
00:13:52.440 --> 00:13:54.920
Do you know what they do to traitors?

142
00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:56.570
You're right.

143
00:13:56.570 --> 00:13:59.780
My apologies. But let me ask you this.

144
00:14:00.150 --> 00:14:01.700
Sentomaru?

145
00:14:01.700 --> 00:14:04.660
Can't you do this one teensy favor for me?

146
00:14:05.030 --> 00:14:08.520
The man who saved you from poverty?

147
00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.410
All those years ago?

148
00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:14.290
Wow! No pressure, huh?

149
00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:23.930
Is he going to attack us?

150
00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:27.390
Three seraphim.

151
00:14:27.720 --> 00:14:30.060
I'm not looking forward to this.

152
00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:32.480
S-Bear!

153
00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:33.690
Thin out their numbers!

154
00:14:35.150 --> 00:14:37.270
S-Bear! Don't move!

155
00:14:38.690 --> 00:14:41.280
We can't beat them. Not like this.

156
00:14:41.280 --> 00:14:42.530
Go, S-Bear!

157
00:14:42.530 --> 00:14:44.490
Take out CP0. They're the enemy!

158
00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.340
Retreat!

159
00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:02.840
We need a new plan, and fast.

160
00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:03.630
No kidding.

161
00:15:04.010 --> 00:15:08.600
So the issue is that Sentomaru outranks
the Authority Chips we're carrying?

162
00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:09.720
That's right.

163
00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:16.600
The system of control is a hierarchy. If someone who's higher
ranked gives an order, that's the order the seraphim will follow.

164
00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:20.770
The highest on the authority chain
are the Five Elders.

165
00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.740
The second highest is Dr. Vegapunk.

166
00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.780
The third is Sentomaru.

167
00:15:29.160 --> 00:15:30.620
<b>Authority Chip</b>

168
00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:34.080
And Authority Chip holders
like us are the fourth.

169
00:15:34.460 --> 00:15:38.750
No matter what we do, Sentomaru's commands
will always be prioritized!

170
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:43.380
Then why don't we make a call to the Five Elders
and have them take control?

171
00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.720
It doesn't work that way.

172
00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:47.380
Pacifistas have to receive
their commands directly.

173
00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:53.430
They won't react to a transponder snail,
Even if it's the Five Elders calling!

174
00:15:55.390 --> 00:15:57.900
Then what are we supposed to do?

175
00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:01.400
The seraphim are valuable Government property,
We can't just destroy them!

176
00:16:01.400 --> 00:16:02.360
Darn it, Lucci.

177
00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:04.820
You really didn't think this through!

178
00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.710
You ready?

179
00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.040
Gum-Gum...

180
00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.560
Time to do this!

181
00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.060
First, S-Snake,

182
00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:41.650
guide Straw Hat and his friends
to the Vacuum Rocket!

183
00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.320
They need to make it to the Frontier Dome!

184
00:16:44.860 --> 00:16:46.820
S-Hawk, S-Shark!

185
00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:48.820
Hold CP0 back!

186
00:16:48.820 --> 00:16:52.280
Chopper, do those children look
familiar to you?

187
00:16:52.280 --> 00:16:57.410
Apart from the black wings and the flames,
they all look like former Warlords of the sea.

188
00:16:57.410 --> 00:16:58.540
You're right!

189
00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.750
There's no way that's a coincidence!

190
00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:04.500
The Government must have made
clones out of us.

191
00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:07.840
Hey! Axe Guy!

192
00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.090
It's been a while, old buddy!

193
00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.470
Straw Hat!

194
00:17:15.100 --> 00:17:18.100
Current circumstances aside,
you and I are enemies.

195
00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:20.310
And I have a name!

196
00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:24.020
So, what? You're helping Punk escape?
Do I have that right?

197
00:17:24.520 --> 00:17:26.400
Uh-huh. I like his apple head.

198
00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.230
And he asked.

199
00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.360
Well, that doesn't exactly fill
me with confidence,

200
00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.740
but I suppose you are an Emperor now.

201
00:17:42.420 --> 00:17:44.470
Hand pistol.

202
00:17:49.550 --> 00:17:51.720
Black sky!

203
00:17:52.260 --> 00:17:54.600
That takes care of their commander.

204
00:17:54.970 --> 00:17:58.810
Seraphim! You follow our orders now.

205
00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:01.940
I'm sorry!

206
00:18:02.940 --> 00:18:04.770
I distracted you and now you're dead!

207
00:18:06.190 --> 00:18:07.270
Idiot.

208
00:18:08.030 --> 00:18:09.610
You didn't distract me.

209
00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:11.610
I saw that hit coming.

210
00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:20.500
Ugh! Damn it!

211
00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:28.580
I was so sure...

212
00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:29.840
I blocked in time.

213
00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:41.770
Hurry up and die.

214
00:18:42.520 --> 00:18:45.150
I can't take control until you're unconscious.

215
00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:29.310
I'm sure you thought you had a fine strategy,
overriding our orders to the seraphim,

216
00:19:29.310 --> 00:19:32.690
but all you did was put
a nail in your own coffin!

217
00:19:56.010 --> 00:19:58.840
Gum-Gum...

218
00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:18.780
Lucci.

219
00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:27.160
Chance!

220
00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.830
Hurry, Luffy!

221
00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.880
If we want to save this girl's life, then we have
to get to Vegapunk's lab immediately!

222
00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.920
I mean, it's not like I don't want to, but, uh...

223
00:20:45.270 --> 00:20:48.100
I can't stop spinning!

224
00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:56.570
Whoa! You really can't stop spinning!

225
00:20:58.860 --> 00:21:02.990
Sorry, kids, I'm going underground!

226
00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:08.870
To the factory!

227
00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:40.110
Is there nothing we can do
to stop these things?

228
00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.610
We're losing men to our own weapons!

229
00:21:42.610 --> 00:21:44.120
I shudder to imagine

230
00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:46.550
how strong they'll be once they grow up.

231
00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.300
Hey, Vegapunk!

232
00:21:50.710 --> 00:21:51.670
What's wrong?

233
00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:55.380
Tell me the truth. What is that power?

234
00:21:55.380 --> 00:21:57.750
And what the hell is that Jinbe
thing doin' with it?

235
00:21:57.750 --> 00:22:00.760
'Cause that looks
like the Swim-Swim Fruit to me!

236
00:22:00.760 --> 00:22:02.260
What's the Swim-Swim Fruit?

237
00:22:02.260 --> 00:22:03.640
It's his.

238
00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:08.680
My hard-boiled brother from another mother,
señor Pink, has that power.

239
00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:12.440
I'd recognize it anywhere.

240
00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:19.990
But it's impossible for there to be two
of the same devil fruit,

241
00:22:19.990 --> 00:22:22.820
so that means my bro must have died!

242
00:22:25.620 --> 00:22:27.490
Ah! My poor bro!

243
00:22:27.490 --> 00:22:29.620
So you would think.

244
00:22:29.620 --> 00:22:33.000
But he's not dead.
He's just being held in Impel Down.

245
00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:36.130
Hold up.

246
00:22:36.130 --> 00:22:39.550
Does that mean you found a way
to duplicate devil fruits?

247
00:22:40.960 --> 00:22:44.470
Well, some devil fruits can be copied.

248
00:22:47.390 --> 00:22:50.560
But it only works with zoan-types.

249
00:22:55.190 --> 00:22:58.690
Hm. Though the less said
about Caesar's SMILE experiments, the better.

250
00:22:58.690 --> 00:23:00.900
Yeah. He can go straight to hell.

251
00:23:03.990 --> 00:23:07.240
The SMILEs offer a high risk
and low success rate.

252
00:23:07.620 --> 00:23:11.660
They only work one time out of ten.
And those who aren't granted power

253
00:23:11.660 --> 00:23:16.120
never stop smiling or laughing. They can't
even mourn for their lost loved ones.

254
00:23:16.120 --> 00:23:16.960
It's sick.

255
00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:19.090
Caesar.

256
00:23:19.090 --> 00:23:22.050
Just hearin' his name again makes
me wanna blow chunks.

257
00:23:25.010 --> 00:23:27.260
Oh, aberrations
such as those notwithstanding,

258
00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:32.890
I have not given up. If we had
enough funding, and enough time,

259
00:23:32.890 --> 00:23:36.480
we could replicate any devil fruit in the world!

260
00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:41.190
Oh. I'm not sure if they'll Awaken.

261
00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:47.310
Hm.

262
00:23:48.700 --> 00:23:52.870
I've tried to recreate logia powers,
but I've had no luck.

263
00:23:52.870 --> 00:23:54.770
And yet...

264
00:23:55.230 --> 00:23:57.750
For a Paramythia Fruit, I need only

265
00:23:57.750 --> 00:24:00.630
acquire the Bloodline Elements of its owner.

266
00:24:00.630 --> 00:24:04.380
Then, I can synthesize a special compound
which, when administered,

267
00:24:04.380 --> 00:24:08.220
confers the... devil fruit power
to another person.

268
00:24:11.890 --> 00:24:13.180
Observe!

269
00:24:14.220 --> 00:24:17.230
That's the fluid you see flowing
through the seraphim's arms!

270
00:24:18.400 --> 00:24:20.690
The Green Blood!

271
00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:25.650
Hold up! You made a new kind of blood?

272
00:24:29.030 --> 00:24:30.070
Love-Love...

273
00:24:31.610 --> 00:24:34.410
Beam!

274
00:24:42.040 --> 00:24:48.310
I believe that seraphim represent
the pinnacle of modern scientific possibility!

275
00:24:51.090 --> 00:24:52.850
A...

276
00:25:00.730 --> 00:25:02.900
Do you know what that makes them?

277
00:25:04.020 --> 00:25:07.490
The strongest form of humanity in history!

278
00:25:07.860 --> 00:25:10.200
Is that why the Government got rid of them?

279
00:25:10.200 --> 00:25:14.950
Why the hell would you even make
something stronger than a Warlord, you psychopath?

280
00:25:15.370 --> 00:25:18.160
They're Navy weapons. Killing machines.

281
00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:18.910
Yes.

282
00:25:19.370 --> 00:25:22.170
And sooner or later, they'll be aiming for us.

283
00:25:32.840 --> 00:25:34.680
Hold on, Sentomaru!

284
00:25:36.180 --> 00:25:37.620
Stay back!

285
00:25:39.060 --> 00:25:40.890
This isn't over yet!

286
00:25:53.410 --> 00:25:55.700
Sentomaru, please stay safe!

287
00:25:57.450 --> 00:26:00.660
Now, where did that little friend
of yours run off to?

288
00:26:01.290 --> 00:26:03.170
I don't know!

289
00:26:03.170 --> 00:26:04.750
And he's not my friend!

290
00:26:05.130 --> 00:26:08.210
What a shame. Guess you're all alone, traitor.

291
00:28:15.010 --> 00:28:18.470
Broken!

292
00:28:21.350 --> 00:28:23.810
When did he get so powerful?

293
00:28:26.560 --> 00:28:27.730
Damn it.

294
00:28:31.190 --> 00:28:33.020
I'm losing consciousness!

295
00:28:44.870 --> 00:28:46.830
Follow me! Quickly!

296
00:28:57.180 --> 00:28:58.510
I said, hurry!

297
00:29:01.260 --> 00:29:04.100
This is no time to be dragging
your feet, you fools.

298
00:29:04.850 --> 00:29:06.720
The Vacuum Rocket is right there.

299
00:29:07.770 --> 00:29:09.100
Now get on!

300
00:29:10.060 --> 00:29:11.730
Why, thank you!

301
00:29:11.730 --> 00:29:14.110
You know, you're much
kinder than the real Hancock!

302
00:29:15.110 --> 00:29:16.230
We owe you one!

303
00:29:16.230 --> 00:29:17.860
Much obliged!

304
00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:19.200
What? D-Don't be absurd!

305
00:29:19.700 --> 00:29:22.450
I-I'm just following orders, alright?

306
00:29:27.290 --> 00:29:30.250
Vacuum Rocket departing in one minute.

307
00:29:30.250 --> 00:29:32.790
Oh, come on, we're out of time.

308
00:29:32.790 --> 00:29:36.280
Hurry up!

309
00:29:38.630 --> 00:29:39.920
What do I do?

310
00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:43.930
Attention. Please take caution
while boarding the rocket.

311
00:29:43.930 --> 00:29:45.310
Straw Hat!

312
00:29:47.280 --> 00:29:51.690
Go! And take care of Punk! You hear me?

313
00:29:53.770 --> 00:29:54.690
Okay!

314
00:29:54.690 --> 00:29:56.110
Leave it to me!

315
00:29:58.690 --> 00:30:00.650
No! You're going the wrong way!

316
00:30:03.030 --> 00:30:06.760
Caution. Doors closing in ten seconds.

317
00:30:17.750 --> 00:30:20.250
We're gonna get him off this island.

318
00:30:21.800 --> 00:30:24.390
No matter what. I promise!

319
00:30:35.530 --> 00:30:37.120
Doors closing.

320
00:30:43.070 --> 00:30:45.170
Prepare to launch.

321
00:30:50.620 --> 00:30:51.830
This is so neat.

322
00:30:59.420 --> 00:31:02.300
It's certainly something right!

323
00:31:03.010 --> 00:31:05.470
What happened to Vegapunk?

324
00:31:08.260 --> 00:31:11.140
Where's pigeon guy? Let me out of...

325
00:31:11.140 --> 00:31:13.020
Whoa. Who the hell is this?

326
00:31:13.020 --> 00:31:14.640
It's Luffy. He's just tired!

327
00:31:14.640 --> 00:31:16.400
I'll give you the details later!

328
00:31:16.400 --> 00:31:18.550
How long was I passed out?

329
00:31:19.860 --> 00:31:22.400
Okay, maybe I'll get used to it.

330
00:31:22.400 --> 00:31:23.690
Please shut up!

331
00:31:23.690 --> 00:31:24.450
You shouldn't

332
00:31:24.450 --> 00:31:28.760
Easy does it. You shut up, too, grandpa!
Go back to normal already!

333
00:31:31.280 --> 00:31:36.210
Departing Fabriophase. Entering Labophase.

334
00:31:40.130 --> 00:31:41.250
Transit duration:

335
00:31:42.420 --> 00:31:43.800
Thirty-two seconds.

336
00:31:43.840 --> 00:31:47.800
<b>Inside the Lab</b>

337
00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:46.510
You have arrived.

338
00:31:46.510 --> 00:31:47.800
Already?

339
00:31:47.800 --> 00:31:50.850
All subsequent rockets are canceled.

340
00:31:50.850 --> 00:31:53.140
Labophase under lockdown.

341
00:31:53.140 --> 00:31:55.100
Frontier Dome security system engaged.

342
00:31:55.730 --> 00:31:58.170
Hostile intruder alert.

343
00:31:58.560 --> 00:32:04.030
All researchers, evacuate to the factory
immediately and seal all entry points.

344
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:13.700
Well, I will say this for the man.

345
00:32:14.870 --> 00:32:18.040
He was a faithful bodyguard to Vegapunk.

346
00:32:19.210 --> 00:32:20.670
Until his dying breath.

347
00:32:21.420 --> 00:32:22.380
Such a waste.

348
00:32:22.880 --> 00:32:25.050
Didn't have to end like this, Sentomaru.

349
00:32:25.050 --> 00:32:29.390
Need I remind you, our orders are to wait
for the Navy before making a move.

350
00:32:29.390 --> 00:32:31.470
They can twiddle their thumbs all they like,

351
00:32:31.470 --> 00:32:34.930
<b>Lab</b>

352
00:32:31.930 --> 00:32:34.020
but I won't wait for Vegapunk to escape.

353
00:32:34.930 --> 00:32:37.270
What do they even stand
to gain from killing you?

354
00:32:37.270 --> 00:32:39.940
You're the smartest man in the world,
and you're on their side.

355
00:32:40.350 --> 00:32:43.440
If they do this, it'll be a huge loss for them.

356
00:32:43.440 --> 00:32:44.650
Well, I think so.

357
00:32:44.650 --> 00:32:48.530
But it appears that the higher-ups have
a different perspective.

358
00:32:49.860 --> 00:32:54.660
I certainly made inventions that have been
beneficial to the World Government.

359
00:32:54.660 --> 00:32:58.410
Innovations in navigation technology
using sea prism stones.

360
00:32:58.410 --> 00:33:00.790
Cyborg animal modifications.

361
00:33:01.420 --> 00:33:05.880
Not to mention my research on devil fruits
that's unlocked their secrets.

362
00:33:05.880 --> 00:33:08.800
Or my creation of human weapons
with the pacifistas.

363
00:33:09.760 --> 00:33:11.180
And now, I've

364
00:33:11.280 --> 00:33:14.220
completed the seraphim as well.

365
00:33:14.600 --> 00:33:20.190
Now imagine if you thought I might turn
that frightful intelligence against you. What would you do?

366
00:33:20.520 --> 00:33:21.730
In that case,

367
00:33:22.400 --> 00:33:23.440
there's no choice.

368
00:33:23.650 --> 00:33:24.560
Hm?

369
00:33:25.310 --> 00:33:27.150
I said, I will not!

370
00:33:27.150 --> 00:33:32.490
For the record, I never planned to revolt.
I still need my research funding, after all.

371
00:33:32.490 --> 00:33:36.330
But the powers that be decided
I was trouble, and that was that.

372
00:33:36.700 --> 00:33:40.210
Alas, life gives you lemons,
government tries to kill you for them.

373
00:33:40.210 --> 00:33:42.920
That is not how the expression
goes, and you know it!

374
00:33:43.250 --> 00:33:47.510
Just when I faced this quandary, an Emperor
and his crew appeared before me.

375
00:33:47.510 --> 00:33:49.840
Fate brought us together,

376
00:33:49.840 --> 00:33:50.380
don't you think?

377
00:33:51.510 --> 00:33:53.390
Hold it! You mean you want to join our crew?

378
00:33:53.890 --> 00:33:55.390
Welcome aboard, crewmate!

379
00:33:56.140 --> 00:33:58.220
Super!

380
00:33:58.220 --> 00:34:01.020
Which of my babies do you want to see first?

381
00:34:01.020 --> 00:34:04.480
The Sunny? General Franky?

382
00:34:04.480 --> 00:34:07.320
What? So we have to take him?

383
00:34:07.320 --> 00:34:08.690
Well, this sucks.

384
00:34:09.070 --> 00:34:10.860
Don't you worry, Nami!

385
00:34:10.860 --> 00:34:12.200
I'm on bodyguard duty.

386
00:34:12.570 --> 00:34:14.530
Oh my, what a gentleman.

387
00:34:14.530 --> 00:34:16.450
Thank you, I feel much safer now.

388
00:34:16.870 --> 00:34:17.580
What?

389
00:34:17.580 --> 00:34:20.080
Shut up and unlock
these shitty shoes already!

390
00:34:20.080 --> 00:34:21.410
I wasn't talking to you!

391
00:34:21.790 --> 00:34:24.080
Oh no! Atlas!

392
00:34:24.080 --> 00:34:25.040
This is serious!

393
00:34:25.040 --> 00:34:26.500
She's not moving at all!

394
00:34:26.840 --> 00:34:28.630
Don't worry, we'll save you!

395
00:34:28.960 --> 00:34:32.430
Ready a repair session
immediately! Patient incoming!

396
00:34:32.430 --> 00:34:34.720
Thank you for bringing her in.

397
00:34:34.720 --> 00:34:36.100
You can leave the rest to us.

398
00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:37.810
Of course, good luck!

399
00:34:37.810 --> 00:34:40.560
Hey, screws for brains!
Where the hell is Vegapunk?

400
00:34:41.730 --> 00:34:43.730
I know he's in here somewhere.

401
00:34:43.730 --> 00:34:45.310
Tell me now!

402
00:34:45.310 --> 00:34:47.230
Bonney, stop it!

403
00:34:47.230 --> 00:34:49.340
You need to calm down!

404
00:34:51.690 --> 00:34:54.860
Wait a sec! Is this his lab?

405
00:34:55.180 --> 00:34:57.990
Wow! So cool!

406
00:34:57.990 --> 00:35:00.250
Are you seeing this, Buddy?

407
00:35:01.120 --> 00:35:02.830
That ancient bastard!

408
00:35:03.160 --> 00:35:05.040
I'm gonna make him pay!

409
00:35:09.300 --> 00:35:11.670
Bonney! Wait, where are you going?

410
00:35:15.720 --> 00:35:19.720
I told Vegapunk to turn my father back
to normal, and what did he do?

411
00:35:21.390 --> 00:35:22.980
He sicked bugs on me!

412
00:35:27.100 --> 00:35:29.110
I'm going to Bury him for this!

413
00:35:29.110 --> 00:35:31.730
I don't think the bugs were his fault, though.

414
00:35:32.990 --> 00:35:34.570
Bonney, wait!

415
00:35:34.570 --> 00:35:36.110
We need to stick together!

416
00:35:36.110 --> 00:35:38.320
Hey, come back.

417
00:35:48.630 --> 00:35:51.840
<b>Fabriophase</b>

418
00:35:51.840 --> 00:35:54.720
Our authority chips are finally back in effect.

419
00:35:54.720 --> 00:35:57.220
The seraphim follow our orders now.

420
00:35:57.760 --> 00:35:59.550
Who's ready for a little revenge?

421
00:36:00.260 --> 00:36:02.560
I took down one of the satellites.

422
00:36:03.930 --> 00:36:08.150
Including Vegapunk himself,
there are six more. This might not be easy.

423
00:36:08.150 --> 00:36:11.150
That's assuming we can even get to them.

424
00:36:11.150 --> 00:36:11.980
Trust me,

425
00:36:12.480 --> 00:36:15.850
that defense system is nothing to scoff at.

426
00:36:16.890 --> 00:36:20.450
We'll see how long it lasts against our forces.

427
00:36:20.450 --> 00:36:22.200
Lock down the island.

428
00:36:22.200 --> 00:36:24.160
Destroy every last ship you can find.

429
00:36:25.290 --> 00:36:27.790
No one escapes Egghead on our watch!

430
00:36:37.790 --> 00:36:43.180
Huh. The Straw Hats are protecting
Vegapunk. How nice of them.

431
00:36:44.100 --> 00:36:47.060
Well, I'm sure they'll be a big help.

432
00:36:49.520 --> 00:36:52.520
Too bad. They still won't escape.

433
00:36:56.070 --> 00:36:59.410
They're in for one hell of a surprise, after all.

434
00:37:01.780 --> 00:37:04.700
Alright. Proceed according to plan, boys.

435
00:37:04.700 --> 00:37:07.410
Send every last ship we have...

436
00:37:09.120 --> 00:37:11.210
...to Egghead Island.

437
00:37:18.120 --> 00:37:23.210
Running so long lost track of just how long its been

438
00:37:24.060 --> 00:37:30.570
Collected scars while striving not even trying beneath my skin

439
00:37:31.070 --> 00:37:37.990
But in the back of my head the dream is not dead I remember a map

440
00:37:38.070 --> 00:37:44.280
to a treasure still gleaming its within our grasp

441
00:37:44.420 --> 00:37:51.190
Can you feel my heart Feelings I impart

442
00:37:51.150 --> 00:37:58.300
The promises are there theyre deep down but still primed to share

443
00:37:58.430 --> 00:38:07.410
Peerless dreams kept close the dreams that always matter most

444
00:38:07.590 --> 00:38:13.160
Before we set sail why not raise a toast

445
00:38:13.280 --> 00:38:20.190
So I pen this note to you Dear sunrise Ill see you soon

446
00:38:20.350 --> 00:38:27.380
See the smile I saw the day that I sang this song to you

447
00:38:27.360 --> 00:38:34.430
And regardless of our age these memries will still remain

448
00:38:34.330 --> 00:38:41.540
Wont forget until this wish makes it to you
